From d195b644c3e5cffc359de885c76f4207c65d0575 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 23:09:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(renovate): no hourly PR limit on the staging flow

prPriority sorts branches within one base branch only (Renovate 44.199.2: sortBranches
at the end of lookup(), once per base; process/index.ts concatenates the bases in
baseBranchPatterns order), so on a staging-flow repo every main branch is processed
before every staging branch. Under the default prHourlyLimit of 2 and a Monday-only
schedule, the two main groups take the week's only slots: on 2026-11-02 revogen and
medical-solutions-of-texas each left five staging branches Rate-Limited (lock-file
maintenance, setup-node digest, Node 26, @prismicio/svelte 3, svelte-select 6).

renovate-staging-flow.json sets prHourlyLimit: 0, reaching only the 15 repos that
extend it; prConcurrentLimit (10) still caps open PRs. validate.yml refuses any other
value and any packageRule prHourlyLimit there. renovate-config.json gets a dated
CORRECTION after its 2026-10-24 note instead of an edit.

Patch from reddoorla/reddoor-maintenance (P1-80b; reddoor-workspace decision
2026-11-02-1828-p1-80-staging-majors-rate-limited, answer (c)).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
